# Workflow Notes

## Episode 01 – Meeting Request Form Setup

In this episode, I created a consultation booking form using Google Forms. The goal was to provide a simple way for potential clients to request meetings without sending emails back and forth.

The form collects important information such as:

* Full Name
* Email Address
* Company Name
* Preferred Date
* Preferred Time
* Meeting Type
* Project Details

All responses are automatically stored in Google Sheets, which serves as the central data source for the automation workflow.

---

## Episode 02 – Automated Email Confirmation

After connecting the Google Sheet to n8n using the Google Sheets Trigger node, I built an automated email confirmation system.

Whenever a new meeting request is submitted:

* The workflow is triggered automatically.
* Client information is collected from the sheet.
* A confirmation email is sent instantly.

This removes the need for manual follow-up and ensures every lead receives a professional response immediately.

---

## Episode 03 – Google Calendar Event Creation

In this episode, I integrated Google Calendar into the workflow.

When a Strategy Session request is received:

* A calendar event is automatically created.
* Client information is added to the event description.
* Meeting details are stored in a structured format.
* Scheduling becomes completely automated.

This reduces administrative work and helps prevent missed appointments.

---

## Episode 04 – Smart Meeting Routing with IF Logic

To make the workflow more intelligent, I added conditional logic using an IF node.

Workflow behavior:

* Strategy Session → Calendar Event + Confirmation Email
* Discovery Call → Confirmation Email Only
* Support Call → Confirmation Email Only
* Project Discussion → Confirmation Email Only

This allows different meeting types to follow different business processes automatically.

---

